# dirvec, session 2: encoder + first number

Session 1 delivered the corpus and the ground truth (see NOTES.md). This session produces the first measurement of the claim. No paper text. No storage engineering. No synthetic queries.

## Inputs
- Repo at HEAD: `data/manifest.jsonl`, `data/dirs.jsonl`, `data/gt_structural.jsonl`, `data/selection.jsonl`.
- The corpus itself is not committed. Rebuild it with `python scripts/fetch.py download` (about 5 GB, about 45 min at Zenodo guest rate, resumable). Then `python scripts/manifest.py` must reproduce `data/manifest.jsonl` byte for byte (same sha256 per file). If it does not, stop and report which files differ.

## Session 2 goal
One unified multimodal encoder, chosen by a short pilot. Every file embedded once and cached. Three directory representations plus one file-level baseline. Leave-one-out directory-stage recall@k per image_frac bucket and per query modality. Result table in the repo. NOTES.md updated with the encoder choice and the numbers.

## Encoder
- Candidates, in order: jina-embeddings-v4 (single-vector mode), nomic-embed-multimodal-3b. Both open weights, both take text and images into one space. Record model id, revision, dtype and hardware in NOTES.md.
- Pilot before committing: embed 20 directories (all their files). Sanity check: for each text or table file, rank its own directory's images against all images in the pilot by cosine; report median rank vs random. If neither model beats random clearly, stop and report.
- One input rule per modality label, fixed for the whole study: image -> the image; text, table -> extracted text, first 2000 tokens; pdf_text -> pdftotext output, first 2000 tokens; pdf_scanned -> page renders at 100 dpi, first 8 pages, mean of page vectors; other (office docs) -> converted text via pandoc or python-docx, else skipped and counted.
- One vector per file. Cache to `data/emb/<model>/vectors.npy` in manifest order plus `data/emb/<model>/index.jsonl` (path, modality, ok flag). Never re-embed a cached file.
- Hardware: a GPU with at least 12 GB. If the machine has none, say so before starting; the fallback is a rented GPU (RunPod, Lambda, Colab Pro), not a smaller model.

## Directory representations (the ablation)
For directory D with children C(D), all built excluding the query file:
- a. pooled centroid: mean of child vectors, one vector.
- b. per-modality centroids: mean per modality present in D, up to 6 vectors.
- c. per-modality k-reps: k-means per modality with k = min(3, n_m), up to 18 vectors.
- d. file-level max (baseline, no container layer): every child vector kept; this is the VectorVFS-style walk of the whole tree.
Score(query, D) = max cosine over D's representative vectors. Rank all directories with n(D) >= 3. Leave-one-out means the query file is removed from its own directory before building a, b, c, d for that query.

## Metrics
- recall@k, k in {1, 3, 5, 10}, per image_frac bucket [0,.2) [.2,.5) [.5,.8) [.8,1] and per query modality, for each of a, b, c, d.
- Bootstrap over directories (1000 resamples) for the 95 percent interval of recall@5 per bucket.
- Report the number of queries and directories behind every cell.

## Kill criterion
The claim is that a loses image queries in the high image_frac buckets and b or c do not. If b and c do not beat a on image queries in [.5,.8) and [.8,1] by more than the bootstrap interval, the claim is dead. Report it plainly either way.

## Deliverables
- `scripts/embed.py`, `scripts/eval.py`
- `data/emb/<model>/` (gitignored; the cache is rebuildable from the corpus)
- `results/session2.md`: the table, the pilot numbers, the encoder choice
- NOTES.md: encoder section and results section appended
- Append to this file the exact prompt for session 3.

## Rules
- Ask only at walls: GPU access, model weights that need a login, licence doubt.
- One commit per deliverable. Nothing beyond what is listed.
- No em dashes anywhere in the repo.
