# dirvec, session 4: cost axis

Session 3 confirmed on fresh directories (pre-registered) that pooled centroids lose the
minority modality of a directory and per-modality reps (b, c) recover it (see
`results/session3.md`, NOTES.md session 3). The file-level baseline d is still not beaten.
This session asks whether the container layer buys anything over the flat walk once cost counts.
No paper text. No new encoder. No synthetic queries.

## Steps, in order
1. Fix the 16 .xls files that are tab-separated text: read them as text when xlrd fails. Record
   the rule change; re-embed only those files; report whether any session 3 number moves.
2. Two-stage retrieval on both sets (session 1 and session 3): rank directories with a, b, c,
   keep the top k in {1, 3, 5, 10}, then rank files inside them; compare end-to-end file recall
   and vectors scored per query against the flat walk d.
3. Report index size (vectors per directory) and query time for a, b, c, d on both sets.
4. `results/session4.md`, NOTES.md session 4 section, session 5 prompt appended here.

