# dirvec, session 6: a representative budget

Session 5 ran the comparison on all 2,808 remaining directories of the pool (see
`results/session5.md`, NOTES.md session 5). H5 was not killed: two-stage with c at k = 10 is within
0.001 hit@10 of the exact flat walk d. Its cost clause failed: c scores 0.55 of the vectors, because
c keeps up to 3 k-means representatives per modality group whatever the group's size, and the large
set has 9.70 files per directory. Against flat HNSW the container layer bought no speed, only a few
thousandths of hit@10 at similar query time, for 53 percent more storage.
This session asks whether a representative budget that scales with directory size keeps c's recall
at a real saving. Same set, same cache; no download and no GPU needed.
No paper text. No new encoder. No synthetic queries.

## Hypothesis (fixed now, do not edit after the first eval run)
H6: on the session 5 set, c4, per-modality k-means with k = min(3, ceil(n_m / 4)) representatives
for a modality group of n_m embedded files (unit-normalised centroids, otherwise as c), used as
stage 1 of two-stage retrieval at k = 10, loses no more than 0.01 hit@10 against the exact flat walk
d over all queries and scores at most 0.35 of the vectors.
Kill: H6 is dead if the paired 95% bootstrap interval (1000 resamples over directories) of hit@10,
c4 at k = 10 minus exact d, over all queries lies entirely below -0.01, or if the mean share of
vectors scored per query by c4 at k = 10 is above 0.35. Report it plainly either way.
Secondary, reported, no kill: c2 (k = min(2, n_m)) the same way; c4 and c2 in the session 3 primary
cells (recall@5, c4 - a and c2 - a); c4 and c2 with HNSW over the representatives as stage 1,
against flat HNSW at the nearest query time.

## Steps, in order
1. Add c4 and c2 to `scripts/eval.py` `build()` and to the stage 1 lists of `scripts/twostage.py`
   and `scripts/hnsw.py`. Leave a, b, c and d unchanged. Check that a, b, c and d reproduce
   `results/session5.md` before reading any c4 or c2 number.
2. `eval.py --criterion s3`, `twostage.py --timing --timing-queries 2000` and `hnsw.py` on the
   session 5 set (`--emb jina-embeddings-v4_s5 --manifest data/manifest_s5.jsonl --dirs
   data/dirs_s5.jsonl --gt data/gt_structural_s5.jsonl`). Timing runs alone on the CPU.
3. `results/session6.md`: the hypothesis block copied verbatim, the tables, the verdict. NOTES.md
   session 6 section. Append the session 7 prompt here.

## Inputs
- Repo at HEAD. On the /workspace volume: `data/corpus_s5/` and the cache
  `data/emb/jina-embeddings-v4_s5/` (27,545 rows, gitignored), venv `/workspace/venv`.
- If the volume is gone: rebuild as in NOTES.md sessions 4 and 5 (download about 29 GB, 3 to 4
  hours from Zenodo; embedding about 1.7 hours on a full RTX PRO 6000, 7 hours on a MIG 1g.24gb
  slice). Record 22672636 is restricted on Zenodo and is not part of the set.
- CPU only otherwise. On a pod whose cgroup allows fewer CPUs than `nproc` reports, set
  `DIRVEC_THREADS`, `OMP_NUM_THREADS` and `OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS` to the allowed count.

