# dirvec, session 7: the container layer against flat HNSW at matched time

Session 6 (see `results/session6.md`, NOTES.md session 6) killed H6 on its cost clause: c4, a
representative budget that scales with group size, scores 0.355 of the vectors at k = 10 (limit
0.35) and loses 0.007 hit@10 against exact d, most of it in the minority-modality cells. Against
flat HNSW neither c4 nor c2 buys anything. The one place the container layer still looked useful is
session 5's HNSW over c as stage 1: 0.003 hit@10 closer to exact d than flat HNSW at about the same
query time, a gap no interval has tested, and smaller than the 0.002 by which multi-thread HNSW
builds move between runs. This session tests that gap with a deterministic build and a paired
interval. Same set, same cache; no download and no GPU needed.
No paper text. No new encoder. No new representation. No synthetic queries.

## Hypothesis (fixed now, do not edit after the first eval run)
H7: on the session 5 set, two-stage retrieval with HNSW over the c representatives as stage 1
(ef_search 100, 100 representatives, exact stage 2 over the top 10 directories) has higher hit@10
over all queries than flat HNSW over the file vectors at the matched setting: the smallest
ef_search in {32, 48, 64, 96, 128, 192, 256} whose measured query time in the same run is at least
the two-stage query time.
Kill: H7 is dead if the paired 95% bootstrap interval (1000 resamples over directories) of hit@10,
two-stage HNSW c minus matched flat HNSW, over all queries, does not lie entirely above zero.
Report it plainly either way.
Secondary, reported, no kill: the same for c4 and c2 as stage 1; the same comparison in the
session 3 primary cells P1 and P2; hit@1; storage of each against flat HNSW.

## Steps, in order
1. `scripts/hnsw.py`: a `--build-threads` option (default: as now) and the flat ef_search grid
   above; write per-query hit@1 and hit@10 of every flat and two-stage setting to
   `data/emb/<emb>/hnsw.jsonl`. Leave M, ef_construction, seed, K_REPS and stage 2 unchanged.
   With `--build-threads 1`, run twice and check that the two per-query files are identical, and
   that exact d and the exact two-stage directory lists still match `twostage.py`.
2. The paired comparison (in `hnsw.py` or a small script reading `hnsw.jsonl`): matched setting as
   defined in H7, interval as in H7, for c, c4 and c2, all queries and P1, P2. Timing alone on the
   CPU, one thread, `--timing-queries 2000` as before.
3. `results/session7.md`: the hypothesis block copied verbatim, the tables, the verdict. NOTES.md
   session 7 section. Append the session 8 prompt here.

## Inputs
- Repo at HEAD. On the /workspace volume: `data/corpus_s5/` and the cache
  `data/emb/jina-embeddings-v4_s5/` (27,545 rows, gitignored), venv `/workspace/venv`. Run
  `twostage.py` once first if `twostage.jsonl` is missing (hnsw.py reads it).
- If the volume is gone: rebuild as in NOTES.md sessions 4 and 5.
- CPU only. On a pod whose cgroup allows fewer CPUs than `nproc` reports, set `DIRVEC_THREADS`,
  `OMP_NUM_THREADS` and `OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS` to the allowed count.

