# dirvec, session 8: the modality gap at folder level

This section replaces the seed-robustness brief drafted at the end of session 7. That brief could
not change the systems conclusion: against flat HNSW over the file vectors, a folder layer buys no
speed and no measurable hit@10 (sessions 5 to 7; H7 dead, +0.0006 [-0.0012, +0.0023]). What stands
is the representation result: a pooled centroid (a) loses the minority modality of a folder and
per-modality k-reps (c) recover it (c - a recall@5 +0.238 and +0.233 in the session 3 primary cells
on the session 5 set).
Related work checked on 2026-09-30. Li et al., "Closing the Modality Gap for Mixed Modality Search"
(NeurIPS 2025, arXiv 2507.19054): the image-text modality gap biases ranking in mixed-modality
corpora; their fix (GR-CLIP) subtracts per-modality mean embeddings post hoc; they evaluate single
items only (one image and one text) and name multi-image, multi-text documents as future work.
Grassucci et al., "Closing the Modality Gap Aligns Group-Wise Semantics" (ICLR 2026, arXiv
2601.18525): closing the gap helps group-wise tasks such as clustering. VectorVFS stores per-file
vectors only; "Directory-Aware Query and Maintenance in Vector Databases" (arXiv 2606.16903) uses
directories as path scopes, not as embedded objects. Federated search (resource selection) is the
classic relative of folder ranking and must be cited. Not read: arXiv 2609.33659 (rate limited).
This session asks whether the folder-level loss is the modality gap at work, and whether the
published fix, applied before pooling, gives one vector per folder that recovers what c recovers
with 5.27 vectors per folder.
No paper text. No new encoder. No download, no GPU.

## Definitions (fixed now)
- Input groups, by what the encoder sees. Image inputs: modality image and pdf_scanned. Text
  inputs: text, table, pdf_text and other.
- Calibration split: a fixed random 20 percent of the session 5 directories (seed 20260930,
  stratified by image_frac bucket). Their files are used only to compute the two group means
  mu_img and mu_txt (means of the unit-normalised file vectors of each group) and are never
  queries. The other 80 percent of directories are the evaluation split. All 2,808 directories
  stay ranking candidates.
- Centering: v' = normalise(v - mu_g) for a file vector v of group g. Queries are centered with
  their own group mean, as in GR-CLIP.
- New representations in eval.py build(), all leave-one-out as before:
  - ac: pooled centroid of the centered child vectors, one vector per folder, queries centered.
  - ab: balanced centroid, the mean of the per-group centroids of the uncentered child vectors,
    one vector per folder, queries uncentered.
  - acb: ab on centered vectors, queries centered.
  - cc and dc: c and d on centered vectors, queries centered.
- Modality gap: the distance between the mean image-input vector and the mean text-input vector
  over the evaluation split (Liang et al., NeurIPS 2022), and the mean cosine of same-folder file
  pairs within a group and across groups, before and after centering.

## Hypothesis (fixed now, do not edit after the first eval run)
H8: on the evaluation split of the session 5 set, the centered pooled centroid ac (one vector per
folder) recovers more than half of c's gain over the pooled centroid a in both session 3 primary
cells: for recall@5, (ac - a) - 0.5 * (c - a) > 0 in P1 (image queries in [0,.2) and [.2,.5)
folders) and in P2 (text-like queries in [.5,.8) and [.8,1] folders).
Kill: H8 is dead if, in either primary cell, the paired 95% bootstrap interval (1000 resamples
over directories) of (ac - a) - 0.5 * (c - a) does not lie entirely above zero. Report it plainly
either way.
Secondary, reported, no kill: ab and acb the same way; ac - a over all queries and in the two
majority-modality cells (a fix that wins minority queries by losing majority ones must show
there); cc - c and dc - d everywhere; the modality gap and the same-folder cosines before and after
centering; vectors per folder for every representation.

## Steps, in order
1. The aborted seed-robustness run left edits in the tree; they were moved to
   /workspace/logs/aborted_s8_seed/ and the tree is clean at the commit that adds this section.
   Check git status before starting.
2. Add the calibration split, centering and ac, ab, acb, cc and dc to `scripts/eval.py` as
   options, defaults unchanged. Check that a, b, c and d on the full set reproduce
   `results/session5.md` before reading any new number.
3. `eval.py --criterion s3` on the session 5 set (`--emb jina-embeddings-v4_s5 --manifest
   data/manifest_s5.jsonl --dirs data/dirs_s5.jsonl --gt data/gt_structural_s5.jsonl`) with the
