# dirvec, session 10 (proposed): the same-modality dilution control

Session 9 (results/session9.md) settled the representation question on this set: no single
vector in the encoder's space matches c (H9a alive), two blind centered clusters per folder do
(tb2c, within 0.013 recall@5 of c in every cell, post hoc), and the pre-registered modality-versus-
dilution test could not separate the two because blind k-means recovers the modality partition
(purity 0.88 to 0.99), so H9c died without answering the reviewer's objection. This session
answers it with the control the prior-art report names (reports/prior_art_2026-09-30.md, objection
table, first row): a minority of the same modality, at the same fraction, from the same kind of
foreign source, against a minority of the other modality. Same cache, no download, no GPU, no new
encoder, no paper text. Nothing is fitted on the synthetic folders; the centering means are the
session 8 calibration means.

## Definitions (fixed now)
- Hosts: evaluation-split directories (session 8 split, seed 20260930) whose embedded files are all
  of one input group (image inputs, or text inputs), with at least 6 embedded files. Guests: for
  each host, files from one other evaluation-split directory (a different Zenodo record) that is
  also single-group, drawn so that the guest fraction n_G / (n_H + n_G) is a value drawn uniformly
  from [0.2, 0.5) with seed 20261001; n_G >= 2. Two synthetic sets built from the same hosts, the
  same fractions and the same seed: SAME (the guest directory has the host's input group) and
  CROSS (the other input group). A guest directory serves at most one host per set; the guest's
  remaining files and the guest directory itself are dropped from the candidate list of that set.
  All other evaluation-split and calibration directories stay as ranking candidates unchanged.
- Files: scripts/synth.py writes data/manifest_s10_<set>.jsonl (the guest files' dir field set to
  the host), data/dirs_s10_<set>.jsonl, data/gt_s10_<set>.jsonl (queries: every embedded file of
  each synthetic folder, marked host or guest; leave-one-out as before; the session 5 dedupe
  exclusions kept). The cache is not touched: index.jsonl paths still equal the manifest paths.
- Rows: a, ac, b2, bc2, tb2, tb2c, c, cc, d, dc (eval.py names). Cells per set: guest queries,
  host queries; guest queries split by fraction [0.2, 0.35) and [0.35, 0.5). Metric recall@5 with
  recall@1 and recall@10 alongside; paired 95 percent bootstrap intervals, 1000 resamples over
  hosts (the same hosts in both sets, so SAME and CROSS are paired by host).
- Loss of a representation x on a cell: (d - x) in recall@5.

## Hypothesis (fixed now, do not edit after the first eval run)
H10 (modality, beyond dilution): on guest queries the pooled centroid a loses more against d when
the guest is of the other input group than when it is of the same input group at the same
fraction: loss_CROSS(a) - loss_SAME(a) > 0. Kill: H10 is dead if the paired 95 percent interval
over hosts of loss_CROSS(a) - loss_SAME(a) includes zero. Report the two losses themselves and the
same difference for ac (centering may account for part of it).
Secondary, reported, no kill: the same difference for tb2, tb2c, b2 and bc2 (does a second
representative recover a same-modality guest as well as a cross-modality one); host-query losses
in both sets (what the guest costs the host); losses by fraction bin; the same-folder cosine host-
guest in both sets next to the session 9 within-group and cross-group numbers; the number of
hosts, guests and queries per set; vectors per folder.

## Steps, in order
1. Check git status (clean at the commit that adds this section). Write scripts/synth.py. Check
   that eval.py on the unmodified session 5 files still reproduces results/session8.md (ranks
   identical for a, c, d, ac, cc, dc) before reading any synthetic number.
2. Build SAME and CROSS. Report the counts and the fraction distribution; if fewer than 150 hosts
   have a guest in both sets, say so and run anyway.
3. Run eval.py on both sets once (--calib 0.2 --queries eval --s9 style tables restricted to the
   rows above; a --gt-cells option for the host and guest cells if the cell logic needs it).
4. results/session10.md: the hypothesis copied verbatim, the counts, the tables, the H10 verdict,
   and a plain statement, with numbers, of how much of the session 3 minority-modality loss is
   present with no modality difference at all. NOTES.md session 10 section. Append a proposed
   session 11 prompt here.

## Inputs
- Repo at HEAD. On the /workspace volume: the cache data/emb/jina-embeddings-v4_s5/ (27,545 rows,
  gitignored), venv /workspace/venv, session 9 logs in /workspace/logs/s9_*.md.
- CPU only. On a pod whose cgroup allows fewer CPUs than nproc reports, set DIRVEC_THREADS,
  OMP_NUM_THREADS and OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS to the allowed count.

