# dirvec, session 11 (proposed): the two-vector result confirmed on fresh folders with a second encoder

Sessions 8 to 10 settled what the paper can say about the folder representation on the session 5
set: no single vector in the encoder's space matches c (H9a alive), and two blind centered clusters
per folder (tb2c, 2.00 vectors) match c within 0.013 recall@5 in every cell (post hoc, session 9).
Session 10 (results/session10.md) gave the same-modality dilution control its answer on the
material this corpus allows: H10 survived by little (loss_CROSS(a) - loss_SAME(a) on guest queries +0.180 [+0.021, +0.345]
over 10 hosts), and three quarters of the pooled centroid's loss on a foreign minority appears with
no modality difference at all. The labelled two-vector rows (b2, bc2) could not see the
same-modality minority; the blind two-cluster rows (tb2, tb2c) recovered most of it in both sets.
That does not change the plan; it makes tb2c, not bc2, the representation to confirm.
Two things stand between the tb2c result and a paper claim. It is a post hoc pick from a grid, so
it has never been tested on folders that took part in no selection. And it is one encoder:
jina-embeddings-v4 (Qwen2.5-VL-3B base). This session is a pre-registered confirmation of both.

## Definitions (fixed now)
- Corpus: a fresh draw of Zenodo records that took part in no selection. The pool snapshot
  `data/pool.jsonl.gz` is spent (its 3,609 eligible records went into sessions 1, 3 and 5), so
  `fetch.py select` takes a new snapshot: the session 1 query (files.types image and text, 3 to 60
  files, public, CC0 or CC-BY), the same eligibility, caps and licence rule, the pages beyond the 20
  per year already taken (or the years 2017 to 2026 in descending record order), with every concept
  in `data/selection.jsonl`, `selection_s3.jsonl` and `selection_s5.jsonl` excluded. Target 2,000 to
  2,800 directories, uniform within the eligible pool, seed 20261101; fewer than 1,500 eligible is a
  wall to report, not to work around. Zenodo stays the source for the reasons of session 1 (per-record
  folders assembled by real people, a filterable licence field; NTSB and EPA are PDF containers).
- Ground truth, input rules, dedupe, calibration split (20 percent, stratified, a fresh seed
  20261102) and centering: as in sessions 5, 8 and 9, per encoder (the group means are recomputed
  on the new calibration split for each encoder; nothing else is fitted).
- Encoders: (E1) jina-embeddings-v4, the study's encoder, same revision and input rules as session 5;
  (E2) one CLIP-family dual tower, jina-clip-v2 (open weights, CC-BY-NC-4.0, research use as with
  the Qwen Research License of E1; 8k-token text tower, so file texts are not truncated to 64 tokens
  as they would be under SigLIP or OpenAI CLIP). Chosen over the session 2 runner-up
  nomic-embed-multimodal-3b because that model shares E1's Qwen2.5-VL-3B base and would confirm the
  base model, not the finding. Optional, if the pod has the time: (E3) gme-Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct
  (Apache-2.0), a VLM embedder on a different Qwen generation, as the prior-art report suggests.
  Before E2 embeds the corpus, the session 2 pilot check (20 directories: text to own-directory
  image median rank against random) is run and reported; if E2 fails it (median rank no better than
  random), say so and use E3 as E2. Licence doubt on any encoder is a wall: ask.
- Rows per encoder: a, ac, c, cc, d, dc, bc2, tb2c (tb2 alongside, uncentered). Cells: all, P1, P2,
  M1, M2 as in session 9. Metric recall@5 with recall@1 and recall@10 alongside; paired 95 percent
  bootstrap intervals, 1000 resamples over directories.

## Hypotheses (fixed now, do not edit after the first eval run on the new corpus)
H11a (two blind centered clusters match c, fresh folders): on the new corpus under E1, tb2c is within
0.02 recall@5 of c over all queries and in each of P1, P2, M1, M2. Kill: H11a is dead if in any of
the five cells the paired interval of (tb2c - c) lies entirely below -0.02.
H11b (the finding is not the encoder): under E2, the pooled centroid a loses to c in both primary
cells (c - a interval above zero in P1 and P2, as in session 3), and tb2c is within 0.02 of c by the
H11a rule. Kill: H11b is dead if either part fails under E2.
Secondary, reported, no kill: the same rows under E3 if run; c - a, cc - c, dc - d, bc2 - c in every
cell per encoder; the modality gap and the same-folder cosines per encoder before and after
centering; purity of the blind two-cluster split per encoder; vectors per folder; the session 10
counts of single-group directories in the new corpus (whether a larger dilution control becomes
possible).

## Steps, in order
1. Check git status. New pool snapshot and selection (`fetch.py select`, new options only if the
   page window needs one); report eligible per bucket and the draw. Download (40 workers, md5).
   `manifest.py`, `build_gt.py`.
2. E1 embedding on the full card (session 5: 270 files/min, about 100 minutes for 27,000 files;
   one job on the GPU at a time). E2 pilot, then E2 embedding. E3 only after E1 and E2 are cached.
3. One eval.py run per encoder on the evaluation split (`--calib 0.2 --s9` restricted to the rows
   above); no dev run, nothing chosen.
4. results/session11.md: the hypotheses verbatim, the corpus counts, the pilot, the tables, the
   verdicts. NOTES.md session 11 section. Append a proposed session 12 prompt here.

## Inputs
- Repo at HEAD. A full GPU pod (a full RTX PRO 6000 or equivalent, 32 GB or more): the E1 cache
  alone is 100 minutes of GPU time, and a second encoder doubles it. /workspace volume with the
  venv; the corpus is about 28 GB at session 5 size.
- Zenodo guest rate limits as in session 5 (80 to 120 files/min): about 4 to 5 hours of download
  for 27,000 files, overlapped with embedding as in session 5.

