# dirvec, session 12: description queries and split robustness (replaces the proposed budget-rule session)

Session 11 (results/session11.md) closed the experimental plan the paper needs; the draft is in
paper/main.tex. Its limitations section names two objections that a cheap CPU session can meet
on the caches already on the volume, so this session meets them before the draft is bulletproofed.
The budget-rule question (a representation between two and five vectors that holds across
encoders) stays open and optional; it is secondary here. The pod's Claude Code session is
rate-limited until 2026-10-04, so this session is driven by hand through the pod's command
endpoint; the scripts and outputs are committed as in every other session.

## Definitions (fixed now)
- Query sets on the session 11 corpus (2,597 directories, all ranked): Q_title, the Zenodo record
  title of each directory, from data/pool_s11.jsonl.gz; Q_desc, the title followed by the record's
  description (metadata.description from the Zenodo record API, HTML stripped), for every record
  whose description could be fetched before the eval run. The query is not a file, so the
  directory representations are built from all of the directory's embedded files (no leave-one-out)
  and every directory with at least one embedded file is a candidate and a query.
- Encoders E1 and E2 as in session 11, text through the query-side path, the same 2,000-token cut.
  Centered rows center the query with mu_txt of the session 11 calibration split (seed 20261102),
  the query being a text input; nothing is fitted on the queries.
- Rows: a, ac, c, cc, d, dc, bc2, tb2, tb2c (eval.py builders, scripts/descq.py). Cells: all
  directories; text-heavy directories (image fraction in [0,.2) and [.2,.5)); image-heavy
  directories ([.5,.8) and [.8,1]); and the four buckets. Metric recall@5 with recall@1 and
  recall@10 alongside; paired 95 percent bootstrap intervals, 1000 resamples over directories
  (one query per directory per set).
- Split robustness: the session 11 evaluation of results/session11.md repeated with calibration
  seed 20261103 (the same fraction and stratification), both encoders, the same rows and cells.

## Hypotheses (fixed now, do not edit after the first eval run)
H12a (the loss reaches natural-language queries): on Q_title under E1, the pooled centroid a loses
to c on image-heavy directories: the paired interval of (c - a) in recall@5 over image-heavy
directories lies above zero. Kill: H12a is dead if that interval includes zero.
H12b (the session 11 verdicts do not depend on the split): under calibration seed 20261103, the
intervals of (c - a) in P1 and P2 exclude zero under both encoders, and under E1 no interval of
(tb2c - c) over the five session 9 cells lies entirely below -0.02. Kill: H12b is dead if either
part fails.
Secondary, reported, no kill: H12a's statistic under E2 and on Q_desc; (c - a) on text-heavy
directories and per bucket; (tb2c - c), (bc2 - c), (cc - c), (d - c) and (dc - d) per cell on both
query sets and both encoders; recall@1 and recall@10; the number of records with a description;
the tb2c - c cells under the second seed next to the first.

## Steps, in order
1. Fetch the descriptions (scripts/fetch_desc.py, resumable, one request per second, into
   data/desc_s11.jsonl). Embed Q_title and Q_desc with E1 and E2 (scripts/descq.py embed) into
   data/emb/<emb>/descq_s12.npz.
2. Run the second-seed evals (eval.py as in session 11 with --calib-seed 20261103, tags
   _s12_e1seed2 and _s12_e2seed2).
3. Run scripts/descq.py eval for both encoders and both query sets; write
   /workspace/logs/s12/descq_<encoder>.md.
4. results/session12.md: the hypotheses verbatim, the counts, the tables, the verdicts; NOTES.md
   session 12 section; the draft's limitations and results updated in a later commit.

## The numbers the draft takes from the repo (carried over from the proposed budget-rule section, which stays optional)
- Diagnosis, pre-registered on fresh folders: results/session3.md (session 3 corpus, c - a in P1
  and P2) and results/session11.md "Session 3 primary cells" tables for E1 and E2 (c - a +0.253
  and +0.169 under E1, +0.500 and +0.348 under E2, with intervals).
- Scale and the flat baseline: results/session5.md (2,808 directories, two-stage c within 0.001
  hit@10 of exact d, share of vectors 0.55), results/session7.md (H7 dead: a folder layer buys
  nothing over flat HNSW, +0.0006 [-0.0012, +0.0023]).
- Mechanism: results/session8.md (modality gap 0.361, same-folder cosines before and after
  centering, H8 dead: centering recovers 49 percent in P1), results/session11.md gap table (0.381
  under E1, 0.787 under E2) and the ac rows.
- Remedy and budget: results/session13.md for every single-vector (F1, F2) number: 40 distinct
  single vectors on the test split, none within 0.02 of c in all four cells, each at least 0.042
  below c in M2 (this line said "results/session9.md (22 single-vector variants ...)" until the audit
  of 2026-10-01; session 9's F1 and F2 rows were biased by a ranking bug and its table had 18 such
  rows, not 22); results/session9.md for the F3, F4 and F5 rows, the dev and test tables and tb2c
  post hoc; results/session11.md (H11a and H11b verdicts, the x - c and
  x - d tables per encoder, purity), results/session10.md (the same-modality dilution control:
  loss_CROSS(a) - loss_SAME(a) +0.180 [+0.021, +0.345] over 10 hosts; three quarters of the pooled
  loss present with no modality difference; tb2 and tb2c against b2 and bc2 on SAME).
- Corpus and encoder facts: NOTES.md sessions 1, 5 and 11 part A (Zenodo selection, licences,
  counts per bucket, dedupe, input rules, revisions); reports/prior_art_2026-09-30.md and
  reports/citations_verified.md for related work and the bibliography.

