# dirvec, session 14: a third encoder from another vendor (E3) on the confirmation set

Why this session exists. The draft's limitations name its cheapest point of attack: both encoders
come from one vendor (Jina), and every statement about a second encoder family rests on one model
that is also the weaker cross-modal encoder on these files. This session adds one encoder from
another vendor on another base, on the confirmation set S11, under the session 11 protocol.
Nothing else changes. Ali approved the compute on 2026-10-01 at 19:40 Toronto.

## Encoder E3 (fixed now)
- Alibaba-NLP/gme-Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct, revision 9cfa6413f704a7c1cf5064d240748e10c876b286
  (Apache-2.0), a unified multimodal embedder on Qwen2-VL-2B (E1 is jina-embeddings-v4 on
  Qwen2.5-VL-3B): 1,536 dimensions, last-token pooling, L2-normalised; cited in the draft as GME.
- Inputs: the same `prepare()` as E1 and E2. Texts are cut to their first 2000 tokens with E1's
  tokenizer (the same characters as E1 and E2 read), images are the same decoded RGB, a scanned PDF
  is the mean of its first eight page renders.
- E3 settings, written down before any E3 number: bfloat16; max_image_tokens 768 (E1's pixel cap,
  602,112 pixels) and the model's default min_image_tokens 256; max_length 2200, so a 2000-token
  text keeps the end token the model pools on; no instruction for any input (the model's default
  system prompt), so its query and document paths are the same and the cache is built with
  `--text-mode query` as E1's and E2's were; the model's own `embed()` in batches of 8.
- Environment: the E1 venv with transformers 4.51.3 first on PYTHONPATH (the model's code refuses
  4.52 and later); weights on the pod's container disk. scripts/embed.py (E3 branch) passed a CPU
  smoke test with a one-layer random-weight copy of the model (settings take, 2000-token texts keep
  the end token, odd image sizes go through, unit vectors of 1,536 dimensions); no E3 number from
  real weights has been computed.

## Gate (fixed now)
The session 2 check on the 20 calibration-split directories of S11 that E2's pilot used
(`embed.py pilot --model gme-Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct --manifest data/manifest_s11.jsonl --dirs
data/dirs_s11.jsonl --tag _s11 --calib 0.2 --calib-seed 20261102`). If E3's median rank of
own-directory images for text and table files is not below the random median, stop: no corpus
embedding, no evaluation; report the pilot.

## Hypotheses (fixed now, do not edit after the pilot)
H14a (the loss holds under a third encoder): on the S11 evaluation split (calibration seed
20261102, the session 11 queries), under E3, the paired 95 percent interval of (c minus a) in
recall@5 lies above zero in P1 and in P2. Kill: H14a is dead if either interval includes zero or
lies below it.
H14b (per-modality representatives keep file-level search under E3): no paired 95 percent interval
of (c minus d) in recall@5 over all queries, P1, P2, M1 or M2 lies entirely below -0.02. Kill: H14b
is dead if any of the five does.
Secondary, reported, no kill: recall@5 of a, ac, bc2, tb2, tb2c, c, cc, d, dc in the five cells
(the draft's Table 3 rows), with recall@1 and recall@10; tb2c minus c read by the H11a rule (the
two-vector budget under E3); centering's share of the loss, (ac - a) / (c - a) in P1 and P2; the
gap table (norm of mean image-input minus mean text-input vector, same-folder cosines, uncentered
and centered); purity of blind 2-means; the session 12 title and description queries under E3
(descq.py: H12a's statistic and the per-cell table); E3's ok set against E1's.
Expectation, written before the run, not a kill: the loss holds in both minority cells, of a size
between E1's and E2's if E3's gap lies between theirs; c stays within 0.02 of d.

