# dirvec, session 15: a second CLIP-family dual tower (E4, Nomic) on the confirmation set

Why this session exists. After session 14 the draft's encoder limitation has two parts: both
vision-language embedders are built on Qwen models, and every statement about a CLIP-family dual
tower rests on one model, jina-clip-v2 (E2), which is also the weakest cross-modal encoder of the
three on these files. The draft says the loss grows to 0.35 to 0.50 under a CLIP-family dual
tower. This session tests that on a second dual tower from a third vendor, on S11, under the
session 11 protocol. Ali asked for it on 2026-10-01 at 22:05 Toronto ("run it, make it robust").

## Encoder E4 (fixed now)
- Nomic Embed v1.5 (Nomic AI, Apache-2.0), a dual tower: the image tower
  nomic-ai/nomic-embed-vision-v1.5 (revision e3a725bce72db07ca4adb1d83da08903f3ee02f8, a ViT-B/16 at
  224 pixels) was trained contrastively against the frozen text tower
  nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5 (revision e5cf08aadaa33385f5990def41f7a23405aec398, the last before
  the repository's transformers 5 rewrite; a BERT-style encoder with rotary positions); model code
  nomic-ai/nomic-bert-2048 at revision 7710840340a098cfb869c4f65e87cf2b1b70caca (trust_remote_code,
  code_revision pinned). 768 dimensions. A CLIP-family dual tower in the draft's sense: two
  encoders, one contrastive objective, no cross-attention between the modalities.
- Inputs: the same prepare() as E1 to E3. Texts are cut to their first 2000 tokens with E1's
  tokenizer (the same characters E1 to E3 read), then go through E4's tokenizer with a limit of 8192
  tokens and rotary_scaling_factor 2 (dynamic NTK scaling; the model's code changes nothing below its
  2048 trained positions, checked on CPU: identical vectors for a 1,406-token text with and without
  it). Images are the same load_rgb images through E4's shipped preprocessing (CLIPImageProcessor:
  resized to 224 by 224 pixels without keeping the aspect ratio; its centre crop then removes
  nothing). A scanned PDF is the mean of its first eight page renders.
- E4 settings, written down before any E4 number: float32; text vector = mean of the last hidden
  states over the attention mask, layer norm without parameters, L2 normalisation (the model card's
  recipe, all 768 dimensions); image vector = the first (CLS) token of the last hidden state, L2
  normalised (the model card's recipe). Every text input gets the prefix "search_query: ", the one
  the model card names for text used against images, so files and the title or description queries
  share one text path; the cache is built with --text-mode query, as for E1 to E3 (the pilot also
  reports "search_document: " as its doc mode, for information only).
- Environment: the E1 venv (transformers 4.52.4, einops already installed for E2); weights and
  model code on the pod's container disk (HF_HOME /root/hf_nomic). scripts/embed.py (E4 branch)
  passed a CPU test with the real weights before this brief was committed: both towers load with all
  keys matched, encode_texts and encode_images equal the model card's recipe to 1e-7, embed_rows
  gives unit vectors of 768 for an image, a text, a table, a text PDF and a scanned PDF, and on four
  synthetic images (a bar chart, a line plot, a text page, a red circle) each image's nearest of four
  captions is its own. No E4 number on a dirvec file has been computed.

## Gate (fixed now)
As session 14: the session 2 check on the 20 calibration-split directories of S11 that E2's pilot
used (`embed.py pilot --model nomic-embed-v1.5 --manifest data/manifest_s11.jsonl --dirs
data/dirs_s11.jsonl --tag _s11 --calib 0.2 --calib-seed 20261102`). If E4's median rank of
own-directory images for text and table files (query prefix) is not below the random median, stop:
no corpus embedding, no evaluation; report the pilot.

## Hypotheses (fixed now, do not edit after the pilot)
H15a (the loss under a second dual tower): on the S11 evaluation split (calibration seed 20261102,
the session 11 queries), under E4, the paired 95 percent interval of (c minus a) in recall@5 lies
above zero in P1 and in P2. Kill: H15a is dead if either interval includes zero or lies below it.
H15b (per-modality representatives keep file-level search under E4): no paired 95 percent interval
of (c minus d) in recall@5 over all queries, P1, P2, M1 or M2 lies entirely below -0.02. Kill: H15b
is dead if any of the five does.
H15c (the larger loss belongs to dual towers, not to one model): on the same queries, the loss
under E4 exceeds the loss under E1: the paired 95 percent interval of [(c - a) under E4] minus
[(c - a) under E1] in recall@5, over 1000 resamples of the cell's evaluation directories with
eval.py's cell seeds (scripts/xenc.py), lies above zero in P1 and in P2. Kill: H15c is dead if
either interval includes zero or lies below it.
Secondary, reported, no kill: everything session 14 reported (the Table 3 rows with recall@1 and
@10, tb2c minus c read by the H11a rule, centering's share, the gap table, purity, the title and
description queries, the ok set against E1, the longest E4 text input); xenc.py's statistic for E4
against E2 and E3 and for E2 against E1; xenc.py's per-encoder c - a intervals checked against
eval.py's.
Expectation, written before the run, not a kill: E4's gap is wide like E2's and its loss lies above
E1's in both minority cells; c stays within 0.02 of d.

