# dirvec, session 17: is the minority-modality loss a fingerprint or creator artifact?

Why this session exists. Ali asked on 2026-10-02 (08:43 Toronto) to continue the experiments and to
choose the next step with independent agents rather than one judgment. Four advisors worked alone
(three SIGIR reviewers, a literature and data scout, a practitioner and investor, a methodologist),
and two judges who had not seen the deliberation scored their proposals on a fixed rubric. Both
judges chose the same sequence: first the methodologist's validity checks (this session, CPU only,
on the ranks already on the volume), then model-written folder abstracts against per-modality
representatives (session 18). The checks come first because the methodologist found that file names
alone, which no encoder sees, put the own folder of an S11 evaluation query in the top five 0.700 of
the time (P1 0.617, P2 0.588; char 3-4-gram TF-IDF of base names, leave-one-out), level with the
pooled E1 vector (0.692) and above E1's c in P2 (0.539). Leave-one-out own-folder retrieval may
therefore reward record fingerprints (shared naming, sidecar files, digitization series) as much as
content. Also: the S11 intervals resample directories, while about 47 effective creator families
stand behind the P2 queries; 527 S11 records share a first creator with S5; and descq.py and
typeq.py import eval.py, so no reproduction so far was independent. No c - a number has been
computed on any subset defined below.

## Definitions (fixed now)
- Set: S11, the session 11 evaluation split (calibration seed 20261102), 17,140 queries, ranks from
  sessions 11, 14 and 15 (data/emb/<cache>/ranks_s11_e1, ranks_s11_e2, ranks_s14_e3, ranks_s15_e4).
  Nothing is embedded or re-ranked except by the independent re-implementation (below).
- Family of a folder: the first creator of its Zenodo record in data/selection_s11.jsonl,
  lowercased and stripped (1,814 families over the 2,597 folders).
- Creator-clustered interval: 1,000 resamples of the cell's families with replacement (generator
  seed: eval.py's cell seed plus 1000; cells all 1, P1 50, P2 51, M1 56, M2 57), the recall@5
  difference recomputed over all queries of the resampled families; 95 percent percentile interval.
  The point estimate is the plain difference over queries, as before. Family-weighted estimate
  (secondary): the mean over families of each family's own difference, with the same resamples.
- The directory bootstrap of scripts/validity.py must reproduce eval.py's published c - a intervals
  in P1 and P2 under E1 to E4 exactly; if it does not, the run stops before any new number.
- Filename-only baseline: char_wb 3-4-gram TF-IDF (sublinear tf) of the lowercased base name without
  its last extension, fitted on the embedded files of the ranked folders; a folder's score is the max
  cosine over its files' names, the own folder without the query file; rank as eval.py. "Names
  miss" means rank above 5.
- Same-stem sibling: another embedded file of the query's folder with the same lowercased stem and a
  different extension (a figure and its PDF, an image and its JSON sidecar).
- The four digitization series (named after an exploratory count of P2 queries, before any c - a
  number on them): the families "digital humanities jena", "nona, dronova", "finnish museum of
  natural history luomus, university of helsinki" and "royal botanic garden edinburgh".
- Clean subset: queries the names miss, without a same-stem sibling, outside the four series.
- Independent re-implementation: scripts/indep_eval.py, written on 2 October by an agent from a
  written specification without reading eval.py, typeq.py, descq.py, xenc.py, selftest_ranks.py or
  twostage.py. On the synthetic cache data/emb/synth16 it reproduced eval.py's a, c and d ranks for
  all 17,091 queries. No real vector has been through it.

## Hypotheses (fixed now, do not edit after the first run)
H17a (the loss survives creator clustering): under each of E1 to E4, the creator-clustered 95
percent interval of (c minus a) in recall@5 lies above zero in P1 and in P2 (all evaluation
queries). Kill: dead under an encoder if either interval includes zero or lies below it. The paper
keeps "under all four encoders" only if it holds under all four.
H17b (the loss is not fingerprint matching): on the clean subset, under E1 and under E3, (c minus a)
in recall@5 is at least +0.05 and its creator-clustered interval lies above zero, in P1 and in P2.
Kill: dead if either condition fails in either cell under either encoder. E2 and E4 reported.
H17c (the metric reproduces): indep_eval.py on the E1 cache gives, for rows a, c and d, recall@5 equal
to eval.py's at three decimals in all, P1, P2, M1 and M2, and identical ranks for at least 99 percent
of the queries of each row (a few exact ties between twin files in different folders may round
differently). Kill: dead otherwise; then nothing else is read until the difference is explained.
Secondary, reported, no kill: c - a on each component subset (names miss; no sibling; not the four
series) and in M1 and M2; family-weighted estimates; families and effective families per cell; the
filename-only baseline with its pooled form; c - d under clustering for E1 to E4 (does any interval
fall entirely below -0.02, the within-0.02 claim); tb2c - c under E1 by the H11a rule under
clustering; the E4 - E1 and E2 - E1 loss differences (H15c) under clustering, and the directory form
checked against the published +0.189 and +0.265; the title and description queries (descq.py rerun
with a new option that writes per-query ranks and changes no number; the E1 H12a statistic must
reproduce +0.182 [+0.158, +0.206]): c - a on image-heavy and text-heavy folders under clustering, and
on the title queries that a filename-only router misses; S3 and S5 under E1, clustered c - a, if
their ranks files are on the volume.
Expectation, written before the run, not a kill: H17a holds under all four (the effects are far from
zero) but the P2 intervals widen; the loss shrinks on the clean subset and stays above +0.05 under E1
and E3; H17c holds.

## Decision rule for session 18 (fixed now)
- H17a, H17b and H17c hold: session 18 is the judges' modified Proposal 3: one model-written abstract
  per folder (an OpenViking-style L0 and L1 from captions and text heads, no digits, IDs, title or
  description, file names cut to words) against a, c and d on title queries, plus member-description
  queries written by a VLM outside the Qwen family with the target kept in its folder; caption-for-
  image rows; BM25 and filename rows; creator-clustered intervals. Pre-registered after this session.
- H17b dies: session 18 is the methodologist's member-description experiment as proposed, and the
  paper's leave-one-out result becomes a robustness section.
- H17c dies: stop; find and fix the difference before anything else.

## Steps, in order
1. Commit this brief, scripts/indep_eval.py, scripts/validity.py, the descq.py --dump-ranks option and
   the driver scripts/s17_run.sh before anything runs. validity.py passed a test on the synthetic
   cache (every section, the S3 and S5 light mode, and the H17c comparison).
2. Check the RunPod balance and the Claude limits. Resume the MIG pod bmao44n64ohrwp, or one of the
   identical MIG pods with the same volume (4ldg1eyjoupfme, gsnfcrhg4j1139, 31dj9o3kjbhwzc;
   $0.59/h) if it has no free GPU. Run setup_pod.sh; start the watcher with a deadline 90 minutes
   after the resume and the markers /workspace/logs/s17/DONE and FAILED.
3. git pull, then bash scripts/s17_run.sh as a background job; it writes
   results/session17_outputs.md, commits and pushes it, and writes DONE.
4. Confirm the pod stopped. results/session17.md (this block verbatim, the verdicts, the
   secondaries), NOTES.md, each as its own commit.

## Inputs and budget
- On the volume: the four S11 caches and ranks files, descq_s12.npz per cache, the E1 venv. Expected
