# dirvec, session 24: a second draw of GitHub directories, sized for the owner minimum

Why this session exists. Session 19's primary test came out inconclusive by one rule alone. Its two
cells hold 86 and 98 owners and its brief requires 100, so H19a cannot be read, and the rule is not
relaxed after the fact. This session draws again under session 19's rules, from repositories that
session 19 did not read, with twice the mixed directories, and reads the same tests on the new draw
alone. The same owner counts say that session 21's cells on S19 (the minority queries whose folder
is not stored whole) will be smaller still and that session 23's 200 trees leave little room, so
both are amended here before either has produced a number.

When this was fixed. Committed on 5 October 2026 at 04:07 UTC. Session 19's E1 evaluation had
finished on the pod at 03:54 UTC and its table of registered tests had been read there; E4 was being
embedded, E2 had not started, and no number of sessions 21 or 23 existed (neither had started).
Seen of session 19 under E1, all of it:
- H19a, c minus a: P1s 226 queries, 86 owners, +0.193, 95 percent [+0.114, +0.277], 98.33 percent
  [+0.099, +0.295]; P2s 355 queries, 98 owners, +0.166, [+0.093, +0.241], [+0.080, +0.260]. Both
  inconclusive (fewer than 100 owners).
- H19c, c minus d where c differs from d: 5,381 queries, 512 owners, -0.002, [-0.011, +0.006],
  [-0.014, +0.008]. Not inferior.
- H19b, clean: P1s 118 queries, 60 owners, +0.188 [+0.090, +0.293]; P2s 205 queries, 82 owners,
  +0.142 [+0.063, +0.225]. No-code folders: P1s 67 queries, 31 owners, +0.210; P2s 232 queries, 62
  owners, +0.096. All of P1: 500 queries, 334 owners, +0.069 [+0.037, +0.100]; all of P2: 512
  queries, 231 owners, +0.071 [+0.036, +0.107].
- H19d, commit subjects on image-heavy directories: 122 queries, 66 owners, gate passed (d 0.254,
  file names 0.066), c minus a +0.010 [-0.061, +0.078].
This session exists because of those numbers. It is a replication designed after a first result was
seen, and the paper says so. H19a's verdict stays what session 19's brief makes it: inconclusive.

## Definitions (fixed now)
- Everything of session 19 that is not named below is unchanged, word for word: the frame, the
  folder, kept files, eligibility, the mixed rule, at most two mixed and two other directories from
  a repository, ground truth, input rules, rows, the eval.py command line (calibration seed
  20261104, 20 percent of this draw's directories), cells, owner, estimator, intervals, the minimum
  of 100 owners, the readings, the clean subset, kinds, the commit-subject queries. The code is
  session 19's, run under the file suffix _s24 (S19_SFX) with no line changed: fetch_gh.py,
  manifest.py, build_gt.py, embed.py, eval.py, s19.py. The driver is scripts/s24_run.sh.
- Frame. The days go on in session 19's order (seed 20261104) from where its pool stopped after 14
  days. Days are read until the pool holds 13,000 usable repositories, session 19's 5,517 included,
  and 2,500 more per round, at most four rounds, if the scored set is not full.
- Scored set. The usable repositories of the enlarged pool are read in a seeded order (seed
  20261104) and every repository in session 19's harvest log, the 4,322 it read, is passed over. No
  repository and no directory is in both draws; an owner can be. Reading stops at 2,000 mixed and
  600 other directories or 40,000 files. Every eligible directory of every repository read is
  listed in data/ghdirs_s24.jsonl.
- Ranked set: this draw's directories alone. Encoder: E1 alone.
- Pooled estimates (scripts/pool.py, run in the workspace on the per-query files the pod pushes).
  For a test, the queries of both draws that fall in its cell; the mean over owners of the owner's
  mean, an owner present in both draws counted once with all its queries; percentile intervals from
  10,000 resamples of owners. On each draw alone the script must first reproduce the points and
  intervals that s19.py and budget.py printed, or it stops before any pooled number. It is committed
  before any file of this draw is embedded.

## Hypotheses (fixed now, do not edit after the first evaluation of this draw)
Primary family, three tests on this draw, each read on its 98.33 percent interval:
- H24a. H19a's statistic and readings: c minus a in P1s and in P2s under E1. Confirmed if both cells
  are confirmed; replicated with the size open if both are confirmed or present; not replicated at
  the registered size if either cell is below +0.05; inconclusive otherwise.
- H24c. H19c's: c minus d where c differs from d. Not inferior if the lower bound is at least -0.02;
  inferior if the upper bound is under -0.02; inconclusive otherwise.
Secondary, read on the 95 percent interval as in session 19: H24b, the H24a statistic on the clean
subset; H24d, c minus a with the commit subject as the query on image-heavy directories, with
session 19's gate; no-code folders; all of P1 and of P2; cs minus d.
The byte-budget tests on this draw, one family of three on 98.33 percent intervals, with session
21's cells, budget (2,048 bytes), policies and readings: H24e is H21a (sample minus mean, minority
queries whose folder is not stored whole), H24f is H21b (sample minus k-means, all queries whose
folder is not stored whole), H24g is H21c (sample minus the uniform sample, minority, not whole).
Pooled over both draws, reported with 95 and 98.33 percent intervals and the reading its rule gives:
every test above and H21a, H21b, H21c.

## What decides what (fixed now)
- The second source. The paper's claim rests on H24a and H24c, read on this draw alone, since this
  draw was sized after session 19's numbers were seen and session 19's own numbers cannot confirm
  themselves. Session 19 is reported in full beside it: inconclusive by its owner minimum, with its
  estimates and intervals. The pooled estimate is given as the size on this source and carries no
  verdict for H19a or H24a. If H24a is not replicated at the registered size or inconclusive, the
  abstract says so.
- The byte budget. H21a, H21b and H21c on S19 under E1 stay session 21's registered tests and are
  reported as such whatever they say. If a cell of theirs holds fewer than 100 owners, which the
  counts above make likely and no session 21 number has shown, the reading the paper takes for that
  test is the pooled one, with the two single-draw reads in the same table. Where S19 and this draw
  both hold 100 owners and their readings differ, the paper reports both and calls the result not
  replicated.
- Inconclusive is reported as inconclusive.

## Amendment to session 23 (made here, before any tree is read)
Session 23's brief stops its harvest at 200 trees or 22,000 files. Session 19 drew 1,053 owners and
found 86 in a minority cell; 200 trees are at most 200 owners, and session 23's minority cell is a
part of them. The harvest now stops at 300 trees or 33,000 files. Nothing else in session 23
changes. If session 19's pool gives fewer than 300 trees, the run goes on with what there is.

## Steps, in order
1. This brief, scripts/s24_run.sh, the calls in scripts/s19_followup.sh and the new stop size of
   session 23 in one commit, with an OpenTimestamps proof of its id.
2. scripts/pool.py with its reproduction check, committed before this draw's files are embedded.
3. On the pod after session 21: scripts/s24_run.sh (pool, harvest, manifest, ground truth, history,
   commit-subject queries, the corpus pushed before anything is embedded, E1, eval.py, s19.py
   validity), then budget.py on this draw, then session 23. Outputs verbatim in
   results/session24_outputs.md and results/session24_budget_outputs.md.
4. results/session24.md, with the pooled table, and NOTES.md.

## Inputs and budget
- About 21,000 files to embed under E1 and about 8,700 tarballs to read: about four hours on the
  pod, about $2.50 of the balance already there. Session 23's larger size adds about an hour.
  Nothing is bought. If the watcher's deadline (16:41 UTC) would cut session 23 short, the deadline
  is moved, not the run.

## Rules
- Nothing is chosen on the new draw. A step that fails is fixed and resumed (S24_RESUME=1); a
  number seen before a fix is listed among the deviations.
- One commit per deliverable. No em dashes.
